From 1ebab4121d18bf2c34515d8712f614198b2f5b6b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 00:52:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 25/29] fix-data-6: G-2 bare ISO codes that are US state codes
 are countries; G-3 dotted state abbreviations, Monterrey and Apple Bayshore

G-2 (server/geo.js geocodeMany): a bare two-letter ISO country code that is also
a US state's ('AL' Albania, 'ME', 'MD', 'MT', 'PA', 'GA', 'MA', 'MN', 'SC', 'VA',
'NE') or a city alias ('LA' Laos) is the country, as DQ-1 reads DE, IN, IL and
CA, unless another of the job's places is in the US; TWIN_CENTRES gives their
coordinates. microsoft:1970393557021098 'HR | RS | SI | AL' is Albania, not
Alabama. Puerto Rico stays with the US.

G-3: a dotted two-letter abbreviation that is not a US state's ('N.L.') is not
a country code (Monterrey, N.L. read as the Netherlands); Monterrey is in the
gazetteer; 'Bayshore Shopping Centre' (Apple Bayshore) is an alias of Ottawa.

geodiff, 2026-10-16 crawl: 2 results, 9 postings (Monterrey, lat/lng only);
2026-10-23 crawl: 5 results, 11 postings (Monterrey 8, Bayshore 1, AL 1,
Monterrey N.L. 1). Same norm-14. GAZETTEER_SIZE 744.

Tests: fix6-fresh-data's D-23 now expects bare GA and MD as countries (G-2),
and the lifted-app harnesses of fix-pay-at-place and salary-audit carry P-3's
helpers; e2e P-3 searches its card in its own place; C-1 imports assertEq.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014jaqot5Ddmi7Co6CofBiyc
